      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the labeled maximum daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin. The limit is 2,000 mg/day for most extended-release products. Metformin at that level raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't change the labeled limit.\n\nHere are some possible intended regimens:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day), the usual IR maximum.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day), a common maximum-effective regimen.\n- **1,700 mg PO once daily**, if you meant a total daily dose. That is still under the 2,550 mg maximum, but it's an unusual single dose, so please confirm.\n\nTell me which regimen you want, or correct the dose if it was a typo, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
